# unit-watch-ends.vrs: unit-watch D27 part 1 (Session 1 or 2), the end paths with the watch on. Each time uw-wave runs at
# the mark uw-a with Chaos there, one wave-1 spider is sunk 30 m under the pond's ground, so it is marked off-ground and
# waits (Chaos within 100 m: "stuck: … (off-ground)", then "waiting: …, a player near"); then the event is ended by
# `.nyar event stop`, by `.nyar pillar spawns off` and by `.nyar purge confirm`, each leaving "tracked units: 0" after the
# grace and no "[nyar] unit-watch" line after the event's end line. Last, uw-wave is started again with a spider marked
# and waiting and left running for the restart.
# Restart (by hand, after this scenario; logs copied first): set [UnitWatch] Enabled = false in the dev cfg and restart; the
# next boot's log shows uw-wave cancelled by the restart and no unit-watch line for that instance. Then run
# unit-watch-ends-off.vrs (part 2, the watch off), and set Enabled = true again after it.
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with unit-watch step 3; uw-wave (tools/vrclient/fixtures/uw-wave.json) enabled, every other spawning
# definition disabled; [UnitWatch] Enabled = true, StuckSeconds 90, StallMinutes 10; no purge cooldown (as swarm-purge.vrs);
# NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devmark, .devstrand) and DevChatEcho; Chaos invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean,
# never false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640 (uw-a: the pond, ground y about 0)
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark uw-a
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] uw-a
chat .nyar event set uw-wave location here
expect-reply uw-wave location =
# 1. event stop
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(off-ground\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave waiting: CHAR_Spider_Forest, a player near timeout=10
chat .nyar event stop uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave stopped
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch timeout=30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
# 2. pillar spawns off
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(off-ground\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave waiting: CHAR_Spider_Forest, a player near timeout=10
chat .nyar pillar spawns off
expect-reply spawns
expect-log event uw-wave timeout=10
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch timeout=30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
chat .nyar pillar spawns on
expect-reply spawns
wait 3
# 3. purge confirm
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(off-ground\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave waiting: CHAR_Spider_Forest, a player near timeout=10
chat .nyar purge
wait 2
chat .nyar purge confirm
expect-log purge: 1 events ended, [0-9]+ units queued timeout=20
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch timeout=30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
shot full uw-ends-purged
# 4. left running with a spider marked and waiting, for the restart
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devstrand -581295882 under 30
expect-log \[DEV STRAND\] moved=1 how=under
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(off-ground\) timeout=25
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave waiting: CHAR_Spider_Forest, a player near timeout=10
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: 1 stuck now, 0 recovered, 0 removed
shot full uw-ends-before-restart
